# Rust
/target
**/target
# Cargo.lock is COMMITTED, and that is deliberate.
#
# Why: this workspace builds shippable binaries — `zylcode-cli` and the
# `zylcode-desktop` Tauri app — not a library consumed by other crates. For
# applications the lockfile is what makes a build reproducible, and it is also
# the artefact `cargo audit` scans. Without it, every developer and every CI run
# resolves a different dependency graph and an advisory match is not stable.
#
# The lockfile is generated as `version = 3` so it stays readable by the
# workspace's declared MSRV (`rust-version = "1.77"`; v4 needs cargo >= 1.78).
# It is marked `-diff` in .gitattributes so reviews stay about source changes.

